 "verbatim_report": "Based on the visual evidence in the provided frames, here is a description of the creature's body and its motion:\n\n**Description of the Creature and Motion:**\n\n*   **Visible Parts:** The creature is a digital skeleton. Key components are clearly visible: a skull (cranium and jaw area), a long spine, rib cage, pelvic bones, and limb bones (forelimbs and hindlimbs).\n*   **Initial State (Frames 1-5):** The skeleton is resting on the grid floor. The skull is on the left, followed by the torso, and then the legs. The entire structure appears relatively compact.\n*   **Movement Begins (Frames 6-8):** The skeleton starts to move as a single unit. It translates forward and slightly rotates to the right. Crucially, all the parts\u2014the skull, spine, ribs, and legs\u2014maintain their relative positions to each other during this movement. There is no articulation of the joints, nor does any part detach.\n*   **Carried Motion (Frames 9-12):** The skeleton is lifted off the ground while maintaining its rigid internal structure. It moves through the air as one cohesive object, rotating and translating. The relationship between the skull, the ribcage, and the legs does not change.\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nThe skeleton reads as **ONE CONNECTED PHYSICAL ANIMAL** being moved and carried by physics.\n\nThis is evidenced by the fact that all the bones move together as a single, rigid unit. There is no separation between the skull, spine, ribs, or limbs at any point. The internal geometry remains constant while the entire object translates and rotates through the space.",
